<title>UK: Trinity H1 profits up, but warns on outlook.</title>
<headline>Trinity H1 profits up, but warns on outlook.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to July 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.7		    vs 9.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.8		    vs 2.6</p>
<p> Pretax		     8.1		    vs 7.5</p>
<p> Turnover		   125.7		  vs 100.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Specialist vehicle manufacturer Trinity Holdings Plc said it expects little growth in earnings per share in the current year, but new products and new market consolidations, coupled with management and productivity improvements, give the company confidence of growth into the future.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 8.71		   vs 7.89</p>
<p> Interest charge	  0.04		   vs 0.08</p>
<p> Tax			  2.66		   vs 2.50</p>
<p> Net taxed		  5.40		   vs 5.01</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 31 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  January 3 1997</p>
<p> Ex-div date		December 23</p>
<p>NOTE - By 0755 GMT, Trinity shares had slumped 64p, or nearly 20 percent, to 259-1/2p in volume of over 280,000 shares.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom + 44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
